{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow. Swami targets SwiftUI’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state graph (computed properties, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than imperative"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"functions, so the two graphs stay aligned. Where a native SwiftUI construct maps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cleanly, Swami uses it. Where Origami’s semantics need a helper — for example the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Interaction patch’s four discrete output ports, or Drag’s momentum + rubber-band"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"physics — Swami ships a helper named after the Origami patch and shaped like it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"title":"Swami","externalID":"Swami"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swami"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"],"title":"Reference","anchor":"Reference"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag"],"title":"Helpers","anchor":"Helpers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/TouchOrigamiExampleView"],"title":"Examples","anchor":"Examples"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/SwiftUICore"],"generated":true,"title":"Extended Modules","anchor":"Extended-Modules"}],"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/OrigamiMappings":{"kind":"article","title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings","role":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Drag":{"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/drag","abstract":[{"text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Drag","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" patch (","type":"text"},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drag","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Drag","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"Drag","role":"symbol"},"doc://samatwork.Sw